# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners enable core.autocrlf by default, which converts
# LF to CRLF in the working tree. A CRLF shell script breaks bash: the CR is
# part of a token, so `then<CR>` and `fi<CR>` are syntax errors and the
# script exits 2 (the release pipeline's "Prepare native toolchain" step).
# Pinning eol=lf keeps the POSIX scripts byte-identical on every runner.
* text=auto eol=lf
